# Testing and Verification

- Identify the relevant test, lint, type-check, build, and static-analysis commands before changing code.
- Add tests for business behavior, boundary conditions, and error paths proportionate to the change.
- Prefer deterministic tests; isolate external systems and avoid real production services.
- For bug fixes, add a regression test when practical.
- Run the narrowest useful checks first, then broader checks when feasible.
- Inspect failures and distinguish regressions from pre-existing failures.
- Report the exact checks run and their outcomes. Clearly list checks not run and why.
- Do not state that the implementation is production-ready based only on compilation or a single passing test.
